    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `bulkSignupWarning` flag with minimal structural impact.\n\n**What I added** (small, cohesive units \u2014 no existing function grew in complexity):\n\n1. **`BulkSignupWarning.java`** (new helper) \u2014 a single static method that counts other owners sharing the owner's `registrationDate` (excluding self by id) and returns `true` when that exceeds 80, `false` otherwise. It mirrors the existing `NamesakeCount`/`RejectOwnerDailyLimit` accumulation pattern.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `setBulkSignupWarning(...)` setter (same as `namesakeCount`, `membershipTier`, `locality`).\n\n3. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated`** and **`RespondWithOwner`** \u2014 one added line each (`dto.setBulkSignupWarning(...)`), so both the create response and the GET response report the flag. Each responder is a one-method class with no surrounding methods, so the change stays cheap.\n\nThe daily count keys off `registrationDate` (the same \"day\" notion the daily-limit rule uses), and self is excluded so the enrichment matches \"owners already created today.\"\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest` (the full suite) passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
